From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:16:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] Test fail-loud commits on logs and WAL directories that
 cannot sync

Decisions 3, 6 and 9 of docs/decisions/durability-policy.md: with durable
commits a log or WAL directory that answers "cannot sync" refuses the
commit before it writes a frame, and the failure is sticky. The degraded
path of Issue2242_UnsyncableLog_Tests, NativeFileSync_Tests,
WalDirectorySync_Tests and UnreadableWalDirectory_Tests moves to
"durable commits=false"; each gains a durable case asserting the refusal,
byte-identical files, exact reads, $database.writeFailure and the
refused next write. WriteFailureAssert collects these checks.

Compact_promotion_on_a_log_that_never_syncs_is_refused_and_keeps_reading_with_durable_commits
stays failing: the promotion's log barrier stops the engine without
recording a write failure, so reads throw afterwards.

